  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 348 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nHighs will warm into the upper 80s to the lower 90s Friday\nthrough the weekend. A few isolated  shower/storms will be \npossible on Friday across portions of southern Missouri but most\nlocations will likely remain dry. \n\nThe ensemble model members show an upper level ridge over the\nplains. There will be the potential for storms to develop across\nthe central Plains and move southeast into portions of the area\nlater Saturday into Sunday. There are still questions on where\nthe storms develop and then how they track with this system. At\nthis time the better potential will be to the north with \nchances decrease to the south into southern Missouri. There \ncould be some locally heavy rainfall if this activity is able \nto move through portions of the area.",
